:: Prologue_Radio {"position":"200,400","size":"100,100"}
<!-- ========================================== -->
<!-- HEADER                                     -->
<!-- ========================================== -->
<center>
    <h1>📻 RADIO: DISPATCH BAND</h1>
</center>
<br>

<!-- ========================================== -->
<!-- RADIO BROADCAST DIALOGUE                   -->
<!-- ========================================== -->
The radio crackles with static, then a voice cuts through—sharp, professional, but bordering on a scream.

<i>"Dispatch, this is Unit 4-Charlie! We are at the precinct! They aren't staying down! I repeat, standard center-mass shots are INEFFECTIVE! Requesting Permission for 'Code Black' engagement!"</i>

<br><br>

A calm, female voice responds: 
<br>
<i>"4-Charlie, Permission for Code Black is GRANTED. All units, be advised: Target neutralization requires complete destruction of the cerebral cortex. Use extreme caution. Do not allow skin contact."</i>

<!-- ========================================== -->
<!-- VISUAL SEPARATOR                           -->
<!-- ========================================== -->
<hr style="border-color: #333; margin: 20px 0;">

<!-- ========================================== -->
<!-- LORE REVEAL & PLAYER THOUGHTS              -->
<!-- ========================================== -->
You hear a code word you remember from training: <b style="color:var(--accent-red)">'PROJECT ODIN'</b>. It was a rumor about a drug intended to bring fatally wounded soldiers back to the fight—a "second life" for the frontline. 

<br><br>

It seems the "Second Life" didn't care about the soldier's mind. Only their hunger.

<br><br>

<!-- ========================================== -->
<!-- ACTION BUTTONS                             -->
<!-- ========================================== -->
<div style="text-align:center;">
    <<button "Back to Room">>
    
        /* Save the radio transcript to the player's Lore Database */
        <<run window.addLore("Police Dispatch Transcript", "Permission for 'Code Black' GRANTED. All units, be advised: Target neutralization requires complete destruction of the cerebral cortex. Use extreme caution. Do not allow skin contact.")>>
        
        <<goto "Prologue">>
        
    <</button>>
</div>